.8966 0.937894 11.6114 1.07983 11.523 1.34327L8.91088 9.13158H0.503157C0.33975 9.13158 0.186521 9.21094 0.0922364 9.3444C-0.0680877 9.57134 -0.0140806 9.88529 0.212865 10.0456L7.00408 14.8432L4.40172 22.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></defs><use clip-path="url(#clip_RatingStar_undefined-2small)" href="#path_RatingStar_undefined-2small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/5879428507">August 24, 2025</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">I did not like this book. I thought the characters and romance was fine if a little cliché and the female lead felt like a 21st century woman. The pacing was also a little off and the climax in particular felt rushed. I also found some of the dialogue to be a little clunky and the plot to be a little predicatable. <br /><br />However, my main issue with this book is its historical setting, as it just made no sense. I couldn't figure out what time period this book is supposed to take place in as the parts in England had a Victorian vibe (with electric street lights, trains, and coming out balls) while the bits in Scotland seemed to take place in the medieval period. This was very confusing, but it also affected the book in another way. Multiple times in the story the phrase 'Scottish law is different from English law' is used and that 'English laws don't matter in Scotland' which is fine if the book has a medieval setting but if it takes place during the Victorian period then it doesn't work. While I am not an expert on Victorian Britain, during that time Scotland didn't have its own parliament, therefore I highly doubt there was much difference, if any at all, between English and Scottish law. This wouldn't have been a problem if the book's whole entire plot did not hinge on the idea that Scottish law and English law were fundamentally different, and so every time this got brought up it took me out of the story completely as I tried to make sense of the setting. <br />I don't understand why this wasn't just set in the medieval period, but as it stands I cannot recommend this book. </span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/55446763?shelf=history" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">history</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/55446763?shelf=read-on-kindle" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">read-on-kindle</span></a><span tabindex="-1"> </span><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/list/55446763?shelf=really-didn-t-enjoy-this" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium"><span class="Button__labelItem">really-didn-t-enjoy-this</span></a></span><span tabindex="-1"></span> <div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--tag Button--medium" aria-label="Show all items in the list"><span class="Button__labelItem">...more</span></button></div></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><p