.6166C4.35092 22.7683 4.37534 22.9352 4.46749 23.066C4.6275 23.2932 4.94137 23.3476 5.16853 23.1876L12 18.3758L18.8317 23.183C18.9625 23.2751 19.1293 23.2994 19.281 23.2486C19.5445 23.1604 19.6865 22.8752 19.5983 22.6117L16.996 14.8432L23.7872 10.0456C23.9206 9.95133 24 9.7981 24 9.63469Z"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6298967871">April 3, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Holy cow. This was an amazing historical read. I have always had a thing for Scotland and love reading about the era when there were lairds and clans and the way of life back then. <br /><br />Charlotte Holloway is promised in marriage to a horrible man named Richard who has already beaten her and treats her like she is absolutely nothing but a breeding cow. She sees no way out as her father won't open his eyes and see the truth, until she meets Conner MacLeod. He is a Laird, a King in his own right, and seems positively smitten with Charlotte, so he becomes her hero.<br /><br />She swats away his advances time and again, even though she feels the pull between them. There have been a lot of rumors spoken to her about Conner and she chose to believe them, even though not one of them had been true. She feels like a fool once she finds out the truth and everything falls into place. I love the chemistry between Conner and Charlotte. They can actually have a real conversation, too. It isn't all about jumping into bed and kissing, which is a nice change from some of these romance books. Because they talk, it is easy to relate with both of them, and they became very real characters for me.<br /><br />Richard never gives up his claim on Charlotte, though. So, she might just need her hero after all. The plot of this story moves at a very nice pace. I didn't fall out of the story at all, but kept reading and flipping pages. I absolutely loved the details and with them it was easy to picture the places in the story.<br /><br />Overall, a very promising debut novel from Ms. McKnight and I look forward to reading even more. I highly recommend this read! It was fantastic!</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i class="Icon LikeIcon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14.4813282,6.41129383 L14.586127,6.97676447 C14.5964421,7.03541935 14.6071117,7.09675198 14.6181364,7.1607667 L14.8551301,8.60363442 L17.440983,8.60363442 C18.1623576,8.60363442 18.8218187,9.01120377 19.1444272,9.65642083 L19.1708204,9.70920723 C19.4523479,10.2722622 19.4523479,10.9350066 19.1708204,11.4980616 L19.118034,11.6036344 L19.1708204,11.7092072 C19.4523479,12.2722622 19.4523479,12.9350066 19.1708204,13.4980616 L19.118034,13.6036344 L19.1708204,13.7092072 C19.4523479,14.2722622 19.4523479,14.9350066 19.1708204,15.4980616 L19,15.8397024 L19,16.1036344 C19,16.7361314 18.6701344,17.3185188 18.1373501,17.6453922 L17.9472136,17.7480616 C17.4795438,17.9818965 16.9638538,18.1036344 16.440983,18.1036344 L9.66834148,18.1034086 C9.31027068,18.6437214 8.696742,19 8,19 L6,19 C4.8954305,19 4,18.1045695 4,17 L4,12 C4,10.8954305 4.8954305,10 6,10 L8,10 C8.60249245,10 9.14276174,10.2664091 9.50943372,10.6878531 L9.58578644,10.6036344 L11,9.18942086 L11,6.75238209 C10.9999468,5.91477784 11.5910613,5.19356674 12.4123594,5.02913493 C13.3640475,4.8385978 14.290004,5.45563256 14.4813282