ath_RatingStar_undefined0small" class="RatingStar__backgroundFill"></use><path class="RatingStar__fill"></path></svg></span></span></div><span class="Text Text__body3"><a href="https://www.goodreads.com/review/show/6298968198">May 10, 2017</a></span></section><section class="ReviewText"><section class="ReviewText__content" dir="auto"><div class="TruncatedContent" tabindex="-1"><div class="TruncatedContent__text TruncatedContent__text--large" tabindex="-1" data-testid="contentContainer"><span class="Formatted">Charlotte just wanted to live her life free. She didn't want to be tied down to any man. But her father was making her find a man this season. So she figured she would just find a man to let her do the things she wanted to. Her father had other plans. He wanted a stable man that would not squander her dowry and leave her desolate and he had just the man. His old friend Richard, who Charlotte detested upon meeting him. Connor came to her rescue and took her away to his lair in Scotland. Little be known to Charlotte Connor had his eye or her and wanted to make her his wife. She figured he was helping a maiden in trouble. Overtime she came to care for him and Love him. But there are people who are trying to keep them apart . But Connor will keep whoever he loves and care safe with his life. I loved how Connor turned out not to be the man she thought. He let Charlotte be who she wanted and loved her for who she was.. Everybody needs a Connor. Can't wait to see more from Kelsey Mcknight. Maybe Penelope's story</span></div><div class=""></div></div></section></section><section class="ReviewCard__tags"><ul class="CollapsableList"><span tabindex="-1"></span><span tabindex="-1"></span></ul></section><footer class="SocialFooter"><div data-testid="actions"><div class="SocialFooter__action"><div class="Button__container"><button type="button" class="Button Button--inline Button--medium" aria-label="Review unliked. Press to like review"><span class="Button__labelItem"><i cl